  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on computing differences between outcomes and a reference value (here, 5 Euros), then evaluating the mean of these differences weighted by their probabilities. The individual does not mention or imply any such calculation. They do not refer to outcome deviations from the sure amount, nor do they discuss favorable or unfavorable differences relative to 5 Euros. Instead, their justification is based on risk perception, certainty, and the one-shot nature of the decision—typical of a risk-averse or certainty-effect rationale. While the reference value in the reason coincides with Lottery A (a sure outcome), the individual does not use this as a benchmark to evaluate gains and losses. The information considered and the justification provided do not align with the structure or logic of the decision reason. Therefore, it is unlikely the reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
